### Await queued requests before finalizing EOF

**Severity:** `high`

EOF can arrive while an already-received request is still queued in `chain`. Finalizing immediately disposes the provider concurrently with that request, so it can fail after the host has supplied all of its bytes. Wait for the serialized chain to settle before shutdown.

```suggestion
  process.stdin.on('end', () => {
    void chain.finally(() => finalize(0));
  });
```
